**Interjection (विस्मयादिबोधक अव्यय)**
Interjection एक ऐसा शब्द होता है जो अचानक आने वाली भावना, आश्चर्य, खुशी, दुख, घृणा, दर्द, प्रशंसा आदि को व्यक्त करता है। यह किसी वाक्य के बाकी भाग से व्याकरणिक रूप से जुड़ा नहीं होता।

---

### 📘 **Definition in English:**

An **interjection** is a word or phrase that expresses sudden emotion or feeling. It is not grammatically related to other parts of the sentence.

---

### 💥 Types of Interjections:

| Type                       | Emotion Expressed         | Examples                |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------- | ----------------------- |
| **Joy** (खुशी)             | Happiness                 | Hurrah! Wow! Yippee!    |
| **Surprise** (आश्चर्य)     | Shock or amazement        | Oh! What! Really!       |
| **Grief** (दुख)            | Sadness or sorrow         | Alas! Oh no! Ouch!      |
| **Approval** (प्रशंसा)     | Agreement or appreciation | Bravo! Well done! Good! |
| **Calling** (पुकारना)      | Attract attention         | Hello! Hey! Hi!         |
| **Hesitation** (हिचकिचाहट) | Uncertainty or pause      | Umm… Er… Uh…            |
| **Disgust** (घृणा)         | Dislike or rejection      | Ugh! Yuck! Eww!         |

---

### 📝 Examples in Sentences:

1. **Hurrah!** We won the match. (खुशी)
2. **Alas!** He is no more. (दुख)
3. **Wow!** What a beautiful painting! (आश्चर्य)
4. **Oh no!** I forgot my wallet. (पछतावा)
5. **Bravo!** You did a great job. (प्रशंसा)
6. **Hey!** Listen to me. (पुकारना)

---

### 🔑 Key Points:

* Interjections are usually followed by an **exclamation mark (!)**.
* They are **not grammatically related** to other parts of the sentence.
* They convey **emotion**, not information.

